        "id": 54,
        "title": "Who needs perfume? The incredible link between body odour and relationships that last",
        "source": "The Guardian - Science",
        "source_id": "guardian_science",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/nov/24/who-needs-perfume-the-incredible-link-between-body-odour-and-relationships-that-last",
        "published_at": "2026-11-24T16:32:08",
        "level": "A1",
        "slot_level": "A1",
        "source_level": "A2",
        "word_count": 443,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "Name: Body odour. Age: Everyone has always smelled of something. Function: Phwoar. This cannot possibly be right. I just sat next to a guy on a bus, and his scent was definitely not phwoar. Let me ask you a question: are you in a long-term romantic relationship with this man? No, of course not. Well, there’s your answer, then.",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "7ac6a74aa4f8f2fcfcd347ca775170b855a582a0",
        "summary": "The longer you have been with your partner, the more likely you are to find their natural scent arousing, according to a study from Radboud University in the Netherlands Name: Body odour. Age: Everyone has always smelled of something.",
